  "worked_solution": "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 15 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-5k+60 \\\\ k-12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5k+60=0 \\\\ k-12=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=12.$",
